From: MacRunner <noreply@macrunner.app>
Subject: [PATCH] build: ensure configure finds libvulkan / libMoltenVK on Apple Silicon

Symptom:
    configure: libvulkan and libMoltenVK development files not found,
    Vulkan won't be supported.
    ...
    dlls/win32u/vulkan.c: error: use of undeclared identifier 'SONAME_LIBVULKAN'

Root cause:
    On Apple Silicon, Homebrew installs to /opt/homebrew/{lib,include}.
    Wine's configure runs basic linker tests with default paths (Apple
    clang does not auto-add Homebrew paths). Without -L/opt/homebrew/lib
    and -I/opt/homebrew/include, configure marks libvulkan/libMoltenVK
    as missing and #undefs the SONAME_* macros that Wine source needs.

Fix:
    scripts/build-wine.sh exports CFLAGS/CPPFLAGS/LDFLAGS/PKG_CONFIG_PATH
    pointing at /opt/homebrew before invoking configure.

Runtime note:
    SONAME_* are passed to dlopen() at runtime. We use absolute paths
    "/opt/homebrew/lib/libvulkan.1.dylib" and ".../libMoltenVK.dylib"
    so dyld doesn't need DYLD_FALLBACK_LIBRARY_PATH set. When we ship
    the engine, these dylibs are bundled and the SONAME is rewritten
    to @rpath/... — see scripts/bundle-engine.sh (TODO).

This is not a Wine source patch — it is captured here so a future
fresh build of engine/wine produces a Vulkan-enabled binary without
manual config.h editing.
